# Graphify ignore file (same syntax as .gitignore).
# Goal: map only first-party game source so the knowledge graph stays small,
# fast to build, and cheap to query. Third-party SDKs and Unity binary/asset
# noise add thousands of nodes with little value for answering questions about
# our own code.

# ---- Unity metadata / binary-ish assets (not source) ----
*.meta

# ---- Sprite / texture / art (no value for code Q&A; would need an LLM key) ----
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.psd
*.tga

# ---- Vendored TextMesh Pro (font licenses, config txt, sprite atlases) ----
TextMesh Pro/

# ---- Third-party SDKs and generated/managed dependency folders ----
Firebase/
Plugins/
ExternalDependencyManager/
GeneratedLocalRepo/
Editor Default Resources/

# ---- Non-source asset / config folders ----
StreamingAssets/
Resources/
Settings/

# ---- Tooling / agent config (not project code) ----
.agents/
.cursor/
graphify-out/

# Keep first-party game code:
#   Poker/           (main poker gameplay + networking)
#   LobbyTutorial/   (lobby / matchmaking)
#   TicTacToe/       (small sample game)
